Here is the complete research report on the Playwright E2E test setup for this project.

---

## 1. playwright.config.ts

**Path:** `/Users/srujansai/Desktop/swa-erp/playwright.config.ts`

```ts
import { defineConfig, devices } from "@playwright/test";

export default defineConfig({
  testDir: "./tests/e2e",
  fullyParallel: true,
  forbidOnly: !!process.env.CI,
  retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,
  workers: process.env.CI ? 1 : undefined,
  reporter: "html",
  use: {
    baseURL: "http://localhost:3000",
    trace: "on-first-retry",
  },
  projects: [
    {
      name: "chromium",
      use: { ...devices["Desktop Chrome"] },
    },
  ],
  webServer: {
    command: "pnpm --dir src/frontend run dev",
    url: "http://localhost:3000",
    reuseExistingServer: !process.env.CI,
    timeout: 120000,
  },
});
```

**Key observations:**
- Test directory: `./tests/e2e` (relative to project root)
- Single project: Chromium only (no Firefox/WebKit)
- Web server auto-starts via `pnpm --dir src/frontend run dev` on port 3000
- 120-second timeout for the dev server to come up
- Retries: 2 on CI, 0 locally
- Workers: 1 on CI, uncapped locally
- Tracing: captured on first retry

---

## 2. All Playwright Test Spec Files

Three spec files were found:

### File 1: `/Users/srujansai/Desktop/swa-erp/tests/e2e/test_login_flow.spec.ts`

